      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.29,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "So actions are important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "for asynchronous code, and in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 9.65,
          "en": "it is a good practice to use actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.65,
          "end": 14.02,
          "en": "Now, I did mention that we have this context, object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.02,
          "end": 16.4,
          "en": "which we get as an argument automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.4,
          "end": 19.59,
          "en": "and that it's full of interesting things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 22.67,
          "en": "Thus far we're only using the commit method though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.67,
          "end": 24.743,
          "en": "So what's inside of context as well?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "Well, we can simply console log context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 30.16,
          "en": "to have a look into it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.16,
          "end": 34.18,
          "en": "So now I log it in increase so if I run, Add 10,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.18,
          "end": 36.55,
          "en": "here is the log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.55,
          "end": 40.42,
          "en": "And we see we got this commit method, which we already saw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.42,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "but we see a couple of other interesting things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.65,
          "en": "Let's ignore route getters and route state for now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 48.92,
          "en": "but let's have a look at dispatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.92,
          "end": 53.363,
          "en": "You can also dispatch a number action from inside an action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "This can be helpful if you're sending an HTTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 61.12,
          "en": "and if it succeeds, you wanna trigger a success action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.12,
          "end": 62.39,
          "en": "if you get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.39,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "you wanna trigger an error handling action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 67.3,
          "en": "Then you could have one action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.3,
          "end": 69.99,
          "en": "that dispatches multiple other actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.99,
          "end": 73.883,
          "en": "in reaction to different results of HTTP request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.05,
          "end": 76.76,
          "en": "You can also access getters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.76,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "in case your action needs some calculated value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 81.563,
          "en": "which would arrive in some getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.92,
          "end": 86.78999999999999,
          "en": "And you can also directly tap into the state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.78999999999999,
          "end": 89.9,
          "en": "in case getting access to the getters might not be enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.9,
          "end": 91.72,
          "en": "You should not manipulate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.72,
          "end": 94.52000000000001,
          "en": "the state from inside the action though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.52000000000001,
          "end": 96.733,
          "en": "Always use a mutation for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.18,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "So that's context and these are actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 102.793,
          "en": "and with state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.42,
          "end": 106.34,
          "en": "mutations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.34,
          "end": 109.18,
          "en": "actions and getters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.18,
          "end": 112.37,
          "en": "we get the core concepts vuex uses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.37,
          "end": 115.97999999999999,
          "en": "to manage state application wide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.97999999999999,
          "end": 118.00999999999999,
          "en": "which you can then use conveniently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.00999999999999,
          "end": 120.263,
          "en": "from inside any component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
